Every other sheet rule is pinned: approval/secret/ask fixtures are byte-checked against the live `renderTuiPrompt`, and the host-menu cue is exercised by the arbitration test. The provider wizard rule (`^┌─ Input ─` / `^┌─ Password ─`) has neither — its headers come from `tui_prompt.dart:141` (`Input`) and `approval_commands.dart:240` (`Password`), but nothing fails if those headers or their frames drift, which silently ships a dead `blocked` rule upstream. `docs/integrations/herdr.md`'s rule table also omits it (it lists only approval/secret/ask/host_menu at 220/220/215/210).

